# Claude Code Rules for ord-api

## Git Commit Policy

**NEVER MAKE ANY COMMITS ON YOUR OWN. ASK THE USER EACH TIME YOU WANT TO CREATE A NEW BATCH OF COMMITS.**

**ALWAYS PUSH IMMEDIATELY AFTER MAKING COMMITS.**

When changes are complete and ready to commit, always:
1. Stop and present a summary of the changes made
2. Explicitly ask the user if they want to commit the changes
3. Wait for user approval before running any git commands
4. Only proceed with commits after receiving explicit permission
5. After commits are successfully created, immediately push them to the remote repository
